  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\nThe simulation transport bar has two new buttons, **Previous op** and **Next op**, between Stop and the slider. Page Up and Page Down do the same steps.\r\n\r\n- **Next op** moves the playhead to the start of the next operation in program order, and pauses the playback.\r\n- **Previous op** moves to the start of the current operation. A second press moves to the start of the one before it.\r\n- The readout already names the current operation (`Contour1 · RAPID · ...`). After a step it names the new operation.\r\n- **Next** is disabled in the last operation. **Previous** is disabled at the start of the first operation. Both are disabled while the stock removal is calculated, as the slider is (#2611).\r\n- The tips (and the AccessKit descriptions) say what each step does, name the target operation and name the key.\r\n- A step across a setup boundary, a tool change or a WCS change is the same step. An operation with no toolpath is not on the timeline, so it is no stop.\r\n- The user guide (`guide/operations` \"Checking\") describes the two steps.\r\n\r\nThe lookup is on `sim::Script` in `camcraft-sim` (`crates/sim/src/sim_steps.rs`: `op_starts`, `next_op_start`, `prev_op_start`, `op_starting_at`), so the stand-alone simulator (#2587) can use the same steps. The UI part is `crates/ui/src/egui_app/sim_steps.rs`; `shell.rs` gets one call.\r\n\r\nAn operation starts at its first segment on the timeline (the connector rapid, when there is one). At that position all moves of the earlier operations are complete. A step is a scrub to that time, so the stock follows the playhead as for a scrub.\r\n\r\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/2608-sim-op-step.md`.\r\n\r\n## Screenshots\r\n\r\nHeadless render at 2x, dark theme, two operations, playhead at 1.0 s.\r\n\r\nBefore (`main`): \r\n<img width=\"2016\" height=\"68\" alt=\"transport\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a23a3bcd-3e95-4adc-a132-1c8def86c13d\" />\r\n\r\n\r\nAfter (this PR): \r\n<img width=\"2016\" height=\"68\" alt=\"transport\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3c01c845-298b-4bca-9637-41ae1dbd5a1d\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pinning tests\r\n\r\n- `crates/sim/tests/sim_op_steps.rs` (8 tests): the value of each start from the segments (`cum[k]` of the last segment of the operation before); the kept `OpStarts` answer as the `Script` lookups; the starts in program order; next from inside operation 1 gives the start of operation 2; previous goes to the current start, then to the one before; no step past the first or the last operation; an operation with no moves is no stop; a non-finite playhead.\r\n- `crates/app/tests/sim_op_step_stock.rs` (2 tests): \"next\" from inside operation 1 (the next operation has another tool) gives the stock after every move of operation 1, the same picture as playback move by move; an operation with no toolpath is no stop, and the stock holds before it as in plain playback (#2280).\r\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/sim_op_steps.rs` (7 tests): a still frame walks no segment (the kept starts are the same `Arc`), and a document change walks the new timeline; click and keys move the playhead and pause; enabled state at the first and the last operation and while held; the tips and the AccessKit description; the shell transport has the steps and the readout names the operation.\r\n\r\n## Readings\r\n\r\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 13 steps, 12 green. The red step is `ui suites: lib`, with four frame-cost tests that fail the same way on clean `main` at 6df70dfc5 (\"the area preview is filled\"). I filed #2762 for them. Each other `ui --lib` test passes.\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- No windowed run. The screenshots are headless.\r\n- The steps do not select the operation in the browser. The decision record gives the reason.\r\n- No run on Linux or macOS.\r\n\r\nMCP: no new command. The playhead is view state, not a document command.\r\n\r\n## Heavy lanes\r\n\r\n`cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` on the final head 235201581 (PROCESS_VERSION 107, #2568). The change in `crates/sim` reaches each heavy target of `motion` and `app`.\r\n\r\n- Lanes that ran: `motion heavy` (33 steps, each target) and `app heavy` (183 steps, each target), after one release build. 217 steps in total.\r\n- Result: 217 steps ok, 0 failed. Wall time 40.7 min.\r\n- The three known-fail steps of #1950 are red as expected: `motion heavy` `the_stock_ring_level_reaches_the_air_planner_with_the_stock` and `the_stock_ring_level_plans_adaptive_with_no_budget_note`, and `app heavy` `the_users_whole_model_bore_roughs_adaptive_on_each_level`.\r\n\r\nChangelog: The simulation has Previous op and Next op steps (Page Up / Page Down) that pause at the start of an operation with the stock that the earlier operations leave (#2608)\r\n\r\nFixes #2608\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
